From c3e63fc2f4b7c5521a5af269fd40f6c55ee9a91b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:38:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(orchestration): transform worker pool and per-file error
 skip

Before: every jssg step ran its transforms one file at a time on one
thread, so heavy codemods took about twice as long as the YAML engine;
one bad file failed the whole step; and the node runtime kept every
parsed tree of a step alive until it ended (1.2 GB on debarrel).

After: batches of 64 files or more run on a pool of worker threads in
both runtimes (node: worker_threads over the shared BatchPlan; quickjs:
one QuickJS context per thread in the host), sized by
CODEMOD_JSSG_WORKERS or the core count capped at 4. A file whose
transform throws or returns an invalid result is skipped and reported on
stderr, as the YAML engine does; `onFileError: "fail"` restores the old
behaviour. The node runtime yields to the event loop before each
transform so addon finalizers run and trees are freed as it goes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
